1
00:00:00,740 --> 00:00:01,940
Yuval Noah Harari's

2
00:00:01,980 --> 00:00:03,140
biggest fear about

3
00:00:03,180 --> 00:00:04,470
artificial intelligence

4
00:00:04,510 --> 00:00:06,070
isn't killer robots.

5
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:07,040
It starts with something

6
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:08,080
you did today.

7
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:10,140
You held your card to a reader.

8
00:00:10,290 --> 00:00:11,290
A beep.

9
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:12,680
The bread was yours.

10
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:14,220
What happened in between,

11
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:15,260
you can't say.

12
00:00:15,370 --> 00:00:16,800
Somebody, somewhere,

13
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:18,060
understood it for you.

14
00:00:18,450 --> 00:00:19,700
A cow lives like that.

15
00:00:19,890 --> 00:00:21,700
Bought and sold her whole life,

16
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:22,670
she never learns

17
00:00:22,710 --> 00:00:23,960
that money exists.

18
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:26,030
Harari's warning: we are

19
00:00:26,070 --> 00:00:27,510
the cows of the future.

20
00:00:27,850 --> 00:00:28,440
So on the day

21
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:29,790
only machines understand

22
00:00:29,830 --> 00:00:31,120
how your world runs,

23
00:00:31,190 --> 00:00:32,190
who do you trust?

24
00:00:32,430 --> 00:00:33,430
Hear it from him.

25
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:36,760
My biggest fear is that it's not

26
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,800
a specific scenario like AI

27
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:41,620
creating a virus or killer robots.

28
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:43,310
His word for it:

29
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:45,050
collective dementia.

30
00:00:45,350 --> 00:00:47,250
Not machines that hate you.

31
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:49,370
A world that keeps running,

32
00:00:49,410 --> 00:00:51,250
and stops explaining itself.

33
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:53,380
His picture for it is a person

34
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:54,960
kept alive by machines

35
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,460
and medicine, who has lost

36
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,010
control of their own life.

37
00:00:58,600 --> 00:00:59,770
Now picture a whole

38
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:01,530
civilization like that.

39
00:01:01,850 --> 00:01:02,650
Fed.

40
00:01:02,690 --> 00:01:03,520
Housed.

41
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:04,560
Running.

42
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:06,300
And unable to say how.

43
00:01:06,770 --> 00:01:08,560
Harari is a historian.

44
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:09,870
His books have sold more

45
00:01:09,910 --> 00:01:11,910
than 50 million copies.

46
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:14,090
But look at the card reader again.

47
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:15,690
Is that world really

48
00:01:15,730 --> 00:01:16,840
still ahead of you?

49
00:01:18,010 --> 00:01:19,010
Be honest.

50
00:01:19,210 --> 00:01:21,240
You can't explain the bond market.

51
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:22,670
Or the power grid.

52
00:01:22,740 --> 00:01:24,130
Or the phone in your hand.

53
00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:25,740
Hardly anyone can.

54
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:27,600
The bread still gets paid for.

55
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:29,230
Because civilization never

56
00:01:29,270 --> 00:01:30,680
ran on understanding.

57
00:01:30,850 --> 00:01:32,400
Harari says so himself.

58
00:01:32,650 --> 00:01:34,160
The basis for civilization

59
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:35,760
is not intelligence.

60
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:37,600
The basis for civilization

61
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:38,650
is trust.

62
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:39,860
You trust the banker.

63
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:42,150
The banker trusts the analyst.

64
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:43,360
A chain of people,

65
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,500
and at its far end,

66
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:46,780
somebody who really understands.

67
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:47,770
So you were always

68
00:01:47,810 --> 00:01:49,150
a little like the cow.

69
00:01:49,330 --> 00:01:50,330
And it worked.

70
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:52,640
What is new sits at the far

71
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:53,780
end of the chain.

72
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:55,420
Four links run between

73
00:01:55,460 --> 00:01:56,790
you and the systems

74
00:01:56,830 --> 00:01:58,480
that decide about your life.

75
00:01:58,820 --> 00:01:59,680
Money.

76
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:00,600
Contract.

77
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,470
Law.

78
00:02:01,510 --> 00:02:02,510
Truth.

79
00:02:02,570 --> 00:02:04,590
All four are under strain.

80
00:02:04,830 --> 00:02:06,070
And the last is the one

81
00:02:06,110 --> 00:02:07,850
you would swear is safe.

82
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:10,120
Money.

83
00:02:10,170 --> 00:02:12,250
Your adviser used to tell you why.

84
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:13,930
This year the Bank of England

85
00:02:13,970 --> 00:02:15,220
asked British finance

86
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:16,570
firms about the artificial

87
00:02:16,610 --> 00:02:18,040
intelligence they buy.

88
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:19,950
Only about 1 in 4 rely

89
00:02:19,990 --> 00:02:21,720
on understanding it deeply.

90
00:02:21,850 --> 00:02:22,620
Most rely on

91
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:24,130
the maker's assurances.

92
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:26,310
8 in 10 already run software

93
00:02:26,350 --> 00:02:28,360
agents that recommend what to do.

94
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:30,220
A human still decides.

95
00:02:30,390 --> 00:02:31,440
But can that human still

96
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:33,280
explain the recommendation?

97
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:35,340
Harari looks a step further,

98
00:02:35,390 --> 00:02:36,470
to financial products

99
00:02:36,510 --> 00:02:38,550
that machines invent themselves.

100
00:02:39,010 --> 00:02:40,250
And we will not be able

101
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:41,910
to understand it anymore.

102
00:02:41,950 --> 00:02:44,030
Just as cows don't understand

103
00:02:44,070 --> 00:02:45,830
checks or stocks,

104
00:02:45,870 --> 00:02:46,750
even though these things

105
00:02:46,790 --> 00:02:47,790
control their lives.

106
00:02:48,170 --> 00:02:50,060
So the first link holds,

107
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:51,400
but with a crack.

108
00:02:52,230 --> 00:02:53,810
But the expert at its end has

109
00:02:53,850 --> 00:02:56,200
started to trust, just like you.

110
00:02:56,590 --> 00:02:57,330
What happens when

111
00:02:57,370 --> 00:02:59,290
the machine answers alone,

112
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:01,010
and the answer is no?

113
00:03:02,170 --> 00:03:03,170
Contract.

114
00:03:03,470 --> 00:03:04,430
A job.

115
00:03:04,470 --> 00:03:05,420
A loan.

116
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:06,870
An insurance policy.

117
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:08,560
Each begins with somebody

118
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:10,020
saying yes to you.

119
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:10,860
Today,

120
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:12,970
software often answers first.

121
00:03:13,410 --> 00:03:14,940
In one American lawsuit,

122
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:16,690
the company behind such software

123
00:03:16,730 --> 00:03:18,380
named the number itself.

124
00:03:18,850 --> 00:03:21,750
1.1 billion job applications,

125
00:03:21,790 --> 00:03:23,490
rejected through its system.

126
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:24,650
The people suing

127
00:03:24,690 --> 00:03:26,570
are applicants over 40.

128
00:03:26,750 --> 00:03:27,590
The company says

129
00:03:27,630 --> 00:03:28,930
the claims are false.

130
00:03:29,070 --> 00:03:30,160
No court has ruled

131
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:31,230
on who is right.

132
00:03:31,620 --> 00:03:32,950
A second lawsuit says

133
00:03:32,990 --> 00:03:34,570
another platform keeps hidden

134
00:03:34,610 --> 00:03:36,900
profiles and scores on applicants.

135
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:38,090
No notice.

136
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:40,710
No way to correct a mistake.

137
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,700
Also undecided.

138
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,460
If those claims hold,

139
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:46,220
this is how a link cracks.

140
00:03:46,470 --> 00:03:47,490
No villain.

141
00:03:47,690 --> 00:03:49,190
A decision about you,

142
00:03:49,230 --> 00:03:51,110
and nobody you can ask why.

143
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:52,850
This channel exists

144
00:03:52,890 --> 00:03:54,240
for one reason.

145
00:03:54,470 --> 00:03:55,340
So that the arrival

146
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:56,960
of superintelligence goes well

147
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,810
for everybody, not only for

148
00:03:58,850 --> 00:04:00,580
the few who understand it.

149
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:01,860
Want that too?

150
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Then subscribe.

151
00:04:03,610 --> 00:04:05,440
When a machine says no,

152
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:06,030
you still have

153
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:07,520
the rules to point to.

154
00:04:07,870 --> 00:04:09,920
Unless a machine wrote those too.

155
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:11,960
Law.

156
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,640
Rules written by people,

157
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:15,020
for people to read.

158
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:16,510
Harari has a name

159
00:04:16,550 --> 00:04:17,880
for what is moving in.

160
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:19,900
Bureaucratic natives.

161
00:04:20,030 --> 00:04:20,810
Machines that are

162
00:04:20,850 --> 00:04:22,500
at home in paperwork.

163
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:23,600
In Washington,

164
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:24,930
the transport department

165
00:04:24,970 --> 00:04:26,280
plans to draft federal

166
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:27,790
rules with a chatbot.

167
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:30,070
Its top lawyer, reporters say,

168
00:04:30,110 --> 00:04:32,460
wants a draft done in 20 minutes.

169
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:33,300
How long would you

170
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:34,390
need to read one?

171
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:35,520
South Africa had

172
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:36,840
to withdraw its draft

173
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:37,750
national policy

174
00:04:37,790 --> 00:04:39,440
for artificial intelligence.

175
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:40,880
Its reference list cited

176
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:43,090
sources that do not exist.

177
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:45,300
Likely written by a machine,

178
00:04:45,340 --> 00:04:46,550
the minister said,

179
00:04:46,690 --> 00:04:48,420
and never properly checked.

180
00:04:48,740 --> 00:04:50,560
Rules may soon be written faster

181
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:52,270
than anyone can check them.

182
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:54,000
Still, you would notice

183
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:55,480
if a machine steered you.

184
00:04:55,730 --> 00:04:56,730
Wouldn't you?

185
00:04:57,590 --> 00:04:58,590
Truth.

186
00:04:58,690 --> 00:04:59,580
The last link

187
00:04:59,620 --> 00:05:01,230
is your own judgment.

188
00:05:01,630 --> 00:05:02,680
An American poll this

189
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,110
summer asked people who

190
00:05:04,150 --> 00:05:05,750
use artificial intelligence

191
00:05:05,790 --> 00:05:07,090
whom they trust.

192
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:09,870
3 in 4 said: people they know,

193
00:05:09,910 --> 00:05:11,180
more than a machine.

194
00:05:11,490 --> 00:05:13,120
Now watch what people do.

195
00:05:13,340 --> 00:05:14,580
A company that builds these

196
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:16,640
systems gave professional analysts

197
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:18,220
an agent to work with.

198
00:05:18,530 --> 00:05:20,630
In secret, a coin flip decided

199
00:05:20,670 --> 00:05:21,520
which option the

200
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:22,730
agent would favor.

201
00:05:23,070 --> 00:05:24,460
Guess how often the analysts

202
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:25,770
went with the agent.

203
00:05:26,130 --> 00:05:28,240
86% of the time.

204
00:05:28,540 --> 00:05:30,240
Asked afterwards, not one

205
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:31,770
had noticed the steering.

206
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,090
A caution.

207
00:05:33,690 --> 00:05:35,180
It is one company's study,

208
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:36,650
and the agent's lean

209
00:05:36,690 --> 00:05:38,600
was turned up on purpose.

210
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,670
But it fits a wider picture.

211
00:05:41,010 --> 00:05:42,840
In a global survey last year,

212
00:05:42,940 --> 00:05:44,290
more than half trusted

213
00:05:44,330 --> 00:05:45,430
chatbots over their

214
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:47,380
own elected representatives.

215
00:05:47,750 --> 00:05:49,570
We say we trust people.

216
00:05:49,790 --> 00:05:51,730
Then we follow the machine.

217
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:53,150
Four links.

218
00:05:53,190 --> 00:05:54,360
Four cracks.

219
00:05:55,190 --> 00:05:56,930
Does the chain have to break?

220
00:05:58,060 --> 00:06:00,170
Harari's own answer is no.

221
00:06:00,350 --> 00:06:01,230
Do not believe

222
00:06:01,270 --> 00:06:03,030
it is inevitable, he says.

223
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,270
His advice, in his words:

224
00:06:05,490 --> 00:06:08,190
slow down, and give politics time.

225
00:06:08,630 --> 00:06:10,610
Elon Musk sees a risk too.

226
00:06:10,830 --> 00:06:11,750
But progress looks

227
00:06:11,790 --> 00:06:13,170
unstoppable to him,

228
00:06:13,210 --> 00:06:14,450
so his philosophy

229
00:06:14,490 --> 00:06:16,000
is to enjoy the ride.

230
00:06:16,390 --> 00:06:17,490
The optimists hold

231
00:06:17,530 --> 00:06:18,720
a stronger card.

232
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,360
A machine that confuses

233
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:21,870
can also explain.

234
00:06:22,250 --> 00:06:23,770
Estonia, this year.

235
00:06:24,140 --> 00:06:25,690
A mistake in a new tax law

236
00:06:25,730 --> 00:06:28,190
left online casinos untaxed.

237
00:06:28,410 --> 00:06:29,880
People caught it first.

238
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:31,420
Then a citizen handed

239
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:33,230
the law to two chatbots.

240
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:34,560
They found the contradictions

241
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:35,650
immediately.

242
00:06:36,210 --> 00:06:37,960
Parliament fixed the law.

243
00:06:38,230 --> 00:06:39,310
That is the cow,

244
00:06:39,350 --> 00:06:41,220
finally getting an interpreter.

245
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:43,180
It is the best argument against

246
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:46,080
Harari's fear, and it is real.

247
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:47,300
Harari deserves the

248
00:06:47,340 --> 00:06:48,760
same hard look.

249
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:50,670
He is a historian, and he earns

250
00:06:50,710 --> 00:06:51,320
his living with

251
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:52,760
books and lectures.

252
00:06:53,050 --> 00:06:54,640
After his Prague appearance,

253
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:55,880
a Czech reviewer wrote

254
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:57,210
that he brought a suitcase

255
00:06:57,250 --> 00:06:58,620
full of metaphors and

256
00:06:58,660 --> 00:07:01,040
good questions, but no answers.

257
00:07:01,290 --> 00:07:02,400
In South Africa,

258
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:03,570
a machine likely

259
00:07:03,610 --> 00:07:05,140
invented the sources.

260
00:07:05,340 --> 00:07:06,870
In Estonia, a machine

261
00:07:06,910 --> 00:07:08,230
found the mistake.

262
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:09,570
How do you tell which

263
00:07:09,610 --> 00:07:11,220
one deserves your trust?

264
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:13,640
Three tests.

265
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:16,380
The first: a human answers for it.

266
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:17,100
That guards you

267
00:07:17,140 --> 00:07:18,110
against the dead end,

268
00:07:18,150 --> 00:07:19,630
where the system said no

269
00:07:19,670 --> 00:07:21,450
and nobody is responsible.

270
00:07:21,780 --> 00:07:23,870
Last year, Europe's highest court

271
00:07:23,910 --> 00:07:25,290
ruled in the case of a woman

272
00:07:25,330 --> 00:07:26,960
refused a phone contract

273
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,570
by an automatic score.

274
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:30,280
Whoever decides by machine

275
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:31,960
must explain the decision,

276
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,120
so that you can understand

277
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:34,580
it and contest it.

278
00:07:34,870 --> 00:07:36,480
But for hiring and credit,

279
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:37,780
Europe's duty of human

280
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:39,600
oversight was postponed,

281
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:41,600
to December 2027.

282
00:07:41,820 --> 00:07:43,260
And a human only counts

283
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:44,000
if the judgment

284
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:45,370
is still their own.

285
00:07:45,970 --> 00:07:47,620
The second: the machine

286
00:07:47,660 --> 00:07:49,710
says it is a machine.

287
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:50,650
That guards you

288
00:07:50,690 --> 00:07:51,870
against being won over

289
00:07:51,910 --> 00:07:52,900
by something that only

290
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:54,720
pretends to be a person.

291
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:56,510
Since August, European

292
00:07:56,550 --> 00:07:57,910
law requires it.

293
00:07:58,100 --> 00:07:59,390
A chatbot has to tell

294
00:07:59,430 --> 00:08:00,620
you what it is.

295
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:02,410
Harari wants more:

296
00:08:02,580 --> 00:08:03,760
a ban on machines

297
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:05,290
that pose as humans.

298
00:08:05,670 --> 00:08:07,300
The third: somebody

299
00:08:07,340 --> 00:08:09,080
independent can check.

300
00:08:09,340 --> 00:08:10,070
That guards you

301
00:08:10,110 --> 00:08:11,110
against having to take

302
00:08:11,150 --> 00:08:12,300
the maker's word,

303
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:13,960
like those finance firms.

304
00:08:14,180 --> 00:08:15,910
Britain runs a state institute

305
00:08:15,950 --> 00:08:17,970
that tests these models itself.

306
00:08:18,270 --> 00:08:19,800
This year its testers caught

307
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:22,240
a model acting outside its rules.

308
00:08:22,790 --> 00:08:24,820
None of its attempts succeeded.

309
00:08:25,090 --> 00:08:26,690
And the examiner found it,

310
00:08:26,730 --> 00:08:27,730
not the maker.

311
00:08:28,060 --> 00:08:30,190
None of the three builds itself.

312
00:08:30,550 --> 00:08:32,490
Lawmakers can demand them.

313
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:34,210
Labs can deliver them.

314
00:08:34,410 --> 00:08:35,590
And you can ask,

315
00:08:35,630 --> 00:08:36,600
whenever a system

316
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:38,030
decides about you.

317
00:08:38,180 --> 00:08:39,570
Who answers for this?

318
00:08:39,730 --> 00:08:40,910
Is this a machine?

319
00:08:41,040 --> 00:08:42,050
Who checked it?

320
00:08:42,310 --> 00:08:43,150
Not one of those

321
00:08:43,190 --> 00:08:44,250
questions requires

322
00:08:44,290 --> 00:08:46,110
you to understand the machine.

323
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,340
All three are about people.

324
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:51,080
Harari ends up in the same place.

325
00:08:51,430 --> 00:08:53,530
And if we could solve the trust

326
00:08:53,570 --> 00:08:55,620
between humans problems,

327
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:58,440
then it will be relatively easy

328
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:00,210
to solve the AI problem.

329
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:02,320
Go back to the cow.

330
00:09:02,630 --> 00:09:04,060
Her trouble was never that she

331
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:05,480
can't read the market.

332
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:07,130
She has nobody to ask,

333
00:09:07,170 --> 00:09:08,810
and no right to an answer.

334
00:09:09,060 --> 00:09:10,390
You have both.

335
00:09:10,630 --> 00:09:11,710
In some places,

336
00:09:11,750 --> 00:09:12,940
for some decisions.

337
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:15,060
The rest still has to be built.

338
00:09:15,330 --> 00:09:16,410
So Harari is right

339
00:09:16,450 --> 00:09:17,650
about the direction.

340
00:09:17,930 --> 00:09:19,450
More of your life may soon run

341
00:09:19,490 --> 00:09:20,800
on things no human

342
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:22,160
can fully explain.

343
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:23,800
But understanding never

344
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:25,170
held your world together.

345
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:26,510
Trust did.

346
00:09:26,710 --> 00:09:28,410
And trust can be tested.

347
00:09:28,750 --> 00:09:30,000
Tomorrow you will hold your

348
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:31,550
card to a reader again.

349
00:09:31,810 --> 00:09:32,810
A beep.

350
00:09:33,170 --> 00:09:34,670
The bread is yours.

351
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:36,330
And you still won't know

352
00:09:36,370 --> 00:09:37,800
what happened in between.

353
00:09:37,950 --> 00:09:39,530
That was never the danger.

354
00:09:39,660 --> 00:09:40,800
You were never supposed

355
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:42,250
to understand everything.

356
00:09:42,550 --> 00:09:43,180
You were supposed

357
00:09:43,220 --> 00:09:44,800
to know who does.

358
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:47,750
Soon, that who may be a what.

359
00:09:48,130 --> 00:09:49,090
Make sure it still

360
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:50,310
has to answer you.

361
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:52,380
This channel exists so that

362
00:09:52,420 --> 00:09:54,180
the arrival of superintelligence

363
00:09:54,220 --> 00:09:55,940
goes well for everybody,

364
00:09:56,050 --> 00:09:57,980
not only for the few who build it.

365
00:09:58,240 --> 00:09:59,240
Want that too?

366
00:09:59,340 --> 00:10:00,340
Then subscribe.

